@page "/"

<PageTitle>GigHaus - House concerts, dead simple</PageTitle>
<HeadContent>
    <meta name="description" content="GigHaus makes hosting house concerts dead simple. Set up a show in minutes, manage your guest list and check people in at the door, free." />
    <meta property="og:title" content="GigHaus - House concerts, dead simple" />
    <meta property="og:description" content="Set up a show in minutes, manage your guest list and check people in at the door. Free for hosts." />
</HeadContent>

<section class="mk-hero">
    <div class="mk-wrap mk-hero__grid">
        <div>
            <p class="mk-kicker">For house concert hosts</p>
            <h1>House concerts, dead simple.</h1>
            <p class="mk-lead">
                Set up a show in minutes, manage your guest list and check people in at the door.
                GigHaus handles the busywork of hosting, and it's free.
            </p>
            <div class="mk-cta-row">
                <a class="mk-btn" href="signup">Host a show</a>
                <a class="mk-btn mk-btn--ghost" href="hosts">See how hosting works</a>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="mk-hero__mascot">
            <Mascot Size="480" Class="mk-hero__image" Animated="true" />
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<div class="mk-band" aria-label="Free for hosts, simple to set up, and GigHaus takes no cut">
    <span>Free for hosts</span><span aria-hidden="true">★</span>
    <span>Simple to set up</span><span aria-hidden="true">★</span>
    <span>No cut of the door</span>
</div>

<section class="mk-section">
    <div class="mk-wrap">
        <h2>Less admin. More music.</h2>
        <p class="mk-lead mk-measure">Hosting should be the fun part. GigHaus gives you one place to run your shows.</p>
        <div class="mk-cards">
            <article class="mk-card">
                <h3>Set up in minutes</h3>
                <p>Add your venue, then the artist, date and guest limit. You get a show page with a link to share.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="mk-card mk-card--gold">
                <h3>One guest list</h3>
                <p>Guests ask for a spot and you confirm them. Your guest limit is enforced for you, so the room never overfills.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="mk-card">
                <h3>Your address stays private</h3>
                <p>The show page only names your city. Guests get the street address by email once you confirm them.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="mk-card mk-card--red">
                <h3>Easy at the door</h3>
                <p>Pull up your guest list on your phone and check people in as they arrive, then go enjoy the show.</p>
            </article>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="mk-section mk-section--navy">
    <div class="mk-wrap mk-setlist">
        <div>
            <p class="mk-kicker mk-kicker--gold">Tonight's set list</p>
            <h2>From spare room to full room in five steps.</h2>
        </div>
        <ol class="mk-steps">
            <li><strong>Tell us about your space.</strong> Your room, your city, how many people fit.</li>
            <li><strong>We say hello.</strong> We review every new venue before it goes live.</li>
            <li><strong>Add your show.</strong> Pick the artist, the date and a suggested donation.</li>
            <li><strong>Share your link.</strong> Guests reserve a spot and you confirm them.</li>
            <li><strong>Open the door.</strong> Check people in, dim the lights and listen.</li>
        </ol>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="mk-section mk-section--cream">
    <div class="mk-wrap">
        <p class="mk-kicker">On the way</p>
        <h2>What we're building next.</h2>
        <p class="mk-lead mk-measure">These aren't ready yet. They're the next things we're adding for hosts.</p>
        <div class="mk-cards mk-cards--three">
            <article class="mk-card">
                <h3>Your mailing list</h3>
                <p>Keep your guests from show to show and build a list of regulars.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="mk-card">
                <h3>Emails and texts</h3>
                <p>Reach your guests by email or text without leaving GigHaus.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="mk-card">
                <h3>Reports and door cash</h3>
                <p>Record the cash you collect for the artist, and see who came and how your shows filled.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="mk-card">
                <h3>Reviews after the show</h3>
                <p>Ask guests for a review after each show, and use the best ones in future publicity.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="mk-card">
                <h3>Merch and extra donations</h3>
                <p>Coordinate online merch sales and extra donations for the artist.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="mk-card">
                <h3>Artist and show info</h3>
                <p>Keep artist and show details together, with an optional Ko-fi connection so artists can be paid directly.</p>
            </article>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="mk-section">
    <div class="mk-wrap mk-free">
        <div class="mk-ticket">
            <p class="mk-ticket__stub">Admit all</p>
            <div>
                <h2>Free. Really.</h2>
                <p>
                    GigHaus doesn't charge you anything, and it takes no cut of what guests give.
                    Guests contribute at the door, and that money supports the artist.
                </p>
                <p class="mk-small">Contributions aren't charitable donations and aren't tax-deductible.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="mk-section mk-section--gold">
    <div class="mk-wrap mk-closer">
        <Mascot Size="256" />
        <div>
            <h2>Got a room? Let's fill it.</h2>
            <p class="mk-lead">Sign up in a few minutes, or tell us about your space and we'll talk it through with you first.</p>
            <div class="mk-cta-row">
                <a class="mk-btn mk-btn--navy" href="signup">Host a show</a>
                <a class="mk-btn mk-btn--ghost" href="contact">Talk to us first</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
